WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Moisture can affect airframes, electronics, motors, connectors, cooling,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.365
navigation sensors, cameras, and lenses.

00:00:06.365 --> 00:00:10.500
Water resistance varies by aircraft and configuration and must be confirmed through

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.880
current manufacturer guidance rather than assumed.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.020
Rain adds water and weight, changes aerodynamic surfaces, obscures imagery,

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.260
and reduces visibility.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.700
Snow can enter components, melt, refreeze, or hide the landing surface.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.840
Ice accumulation can change lift and control and should be treated as a serious hazard.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.765
Fog and low cloud reduce visual range and contrast.

00:00:28.765 --> 00:00:32.100
Aircraft lights may remain visible while obstacles, terrain, other traffic,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.240
and the route are not.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.037
Maintaining sight of one light does not mean the operation remains safe or compliant.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:37.970
Humidity, mist,

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.940
and temperature transitions can create condensation on lenses or inside equipment.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.920
A fogged payload may produce misleading or useless data.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.700
Do not continue merely to complete a planned route when the sensor product has failed.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.515
If precipitation, visibility, or moisture exceeds approved limits, cancel or land.

00:00:53.515 --> 00:00:55.645
Protect equipment during transport and recovery,

00:00:55.645 --> 00:00:59.790
and avoid opening sensitive compartments in blowing rain, snow, dust, or spray.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.720
Wind-driven moisture can reach openings and surfaces that remain protected in calm

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.440
conditions.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.530
Evaluate precipitation and airflow together rather than treating a light shower as an

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.400
isolated factor.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.155
After exposure, power down, inspect, dry, clean,

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:14.755
and document the equipment according to approved procedures.

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:18.020
Address contamination or corrosion concerns before another flight.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.020
A normal landing does not prove that moisture caused no damage.
